14         assertTrue(n.get("customerCode").asText().matches("[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}")); // <REGION>-<HASH8>
15     }
16  }
```
This asserts `customerCode` matches `REGION-HASH8`, which the current `assignCustomerCode` (`CITY3-LAST3-NNNN`) does not satisfy — this is the acceptance target for the redesign.

**`AcceptanceBase.java`** — the base harness. Relevant reusable pieces (no `@Test` methods itself):
- `region(String city)` / `CITY_REGION` map (lines 228-246) — pinned Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD, else `UNKNOWN`.
- `REGION_POSTCODES` map + `validPostcode(city)` (lines 236-237, 252-256) — mirrors the NSW/VIC/QLD ranges.
- `knownOwner(city)` / `withPostcode` / `ownerNode` / `structuredOwner` payload builders (lines 117-142, 260-265).
- `sha256hex` / `shaHex(s, n)` (lines 281-299) — the SHA-256 hashing the `<HASH8>` design expects, upper-cased hex.
- `luhn(String s)` (lines 301-321) — a test-side replica of `CheckDigits.luhn` for asserting `checkDigit`.
- `createOwnerOk`, `fetchOwner`, `extractId` helpers (lines 155-219).

**`AuditLogCapture.java`** — utility (no `@Test`) that captures the `"AUDIT"` logger output via a Logback `ListAppender`; `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(level, ...)`, `count()`. This is the mechanism for asserting the create-audit record from section 3.

